msgid "The front's hatred grows with every ambush, harassing strike, raid and strike against its hordes, and every map event left undone. Its next horde to set out takes all of it, and the front's hatred starts again from nothing. Each time it passes another 100%%, the front's next horde sends a band of %d%% of its troops against the nearest village. A horde that took it leaves %s more camps behind when it is over (the whole part surely, the rest by chance). Ambushes on the front are riskier, and worth more."
